<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine crude oil output rises 8.9 pct in '96.</title>
<headline>Argentine crude oil output rises 8.9 pct in '96.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine crude oil output rose 8.9 percent in 1996 to 45.6 million cubic meters, the Argentine Petroleum and Gas Institute said Friday.</p>
<p>Crude exports rose by 16.1 percent to 18.8 million cubic meters in the same period.</p>
<p>Refined oil output, including that made with imported crude, rose by 5.1 percent to 27.7 million cubic meters.</p>
<p>Natural gas output rose by 13.6 percent to 34.6 billion cubic meters.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
</text>
